    "result_text": "**BUILD SUCCESS** \u2014 all 14 tests pass, including the new `Cp07Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented registration-date support for `POST /api/owners`: when no `registrationDate` is supplied it defaults to the server's current date, and the value is returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format (and a supplied date is preserved).\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `registrationDate` (`type: string`, `format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. The OpenAPI generator maps this to `LocalDate` on the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto`, which Jackson serializes as `YYYY-MM-DD`. Being part of `OwnerFields`, it's both accepted on the request and returned in the `Owner` response.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `LocalDate registrationDate` field mapped to a `registration_date` column, with getter/setter. MapStruct auto-maps it by name in both directions, so no mapper changes were needed.\n\n3. **`function/owner/BuildOwner.java`** \u2014 after mapping the request to an `Owner`, defaults `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when the client omitted it. A supplied date flows through the mapper untouched.\n\n4. **DB schemas** \u2014 added `registration_date DATE` to the `owners` table in all four dialects (h2, hsqldb, postgres, mysql). The hsqldb and mysql `data.sql` seed files use positional inserts, so I appended a `NULL` for the new column to each owner row (h2/postgres already use explicit column lists).\n\nThe test suite runs under the hsqldb profile, which is why the initial run surfaced the positional-insert column-count mismatch; that's now resolved.",
